    followUps: ["Why does an interaction at page load often have the worst input delay?", "How would you budget INP in CI when it is a field metric?"],
    deeper: [
      "Know the thresholds and the measurement: good is 200ms or less at the 75th percentile, poor is over 500ms, and an interaction is measured from input to the next paint, so work deferred until after the paint does not count against it — which is exactly why yielding after the visible update works.",
      "scheduler.yield() continues your task ahead of other queued work, unlike setTimeout(0), which goes to the back of the queue; check current browser support before relying on it and keep the fallback.",
    ],
