      "Where it bites in practice: personalised data accidentally inside a cached scope, which is a data leak between users rather than a staleness bug; cookies() or headers() read deep in a tree silently making a whole route dynamic; and a patch cadence problem — the December 2025 RSC deserialisation RCE meant teams on Next needed same-day upgrades, so the framework is a dependency you must be able to patch fast.",
