      "<Activity> keeps a subtree mounted while hiding it: mode hidden hides it visually, unmounts its effects, and defers its updates to idle time; switching back to visible restores state, scroll and form input without a refetch. That makes tabs, a closed side panel, or a back navigation keep their state — the thing people used to fake with display:none, which kept effects running, or by lifting state up. It can also pre-render a likely next screen in the background.",
