      "The gotchas: an element cannot query itself, only an ancestor container, so you sometimes add a wrapper. And inline-size containment means the container's width no longer depends on its content, so a container that was sized by its content, an inline-block or a shrink-to-fit flex item, collapses. Put the containment on an element whose width comes from its parent.",
